A||||7||RobertVol||Maniffold Replacment Time(how long?)||||5||
Z||000000||RobertVol||10-31-2000||12:26 PM||||How many labor hours does it call for to replace the exaust manifolds on the GT? Thanks in Advance ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||10-31-2000||01:03 PM||||IF none of the bolts snap about 1 hour. Would suggest start soaking all the bolts daily with penetrating oil about a week in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||10-31-2000||06:03 PM||||It took me much longer than one hour, but I pulled the entire exhaust off to get alot more room to work.  Also, the A/C compressor has to come off (leave the lines connected!) to get to the front manifold bolts. This probably took an hour in itself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||10-31-2000||09:34 PM||||Id LOVE to see someone change just the front exhaust manifold in an hour!!!!!!!<BR>It took me about a week........you'll see.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||10-31-2000||10:45 PM||||Ok then If I dont do it myself and Pay a friend who is a mechanic. How many hours? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||11-01-2000||12:32 AM||||If it isn't really that bad I wouldn't bother. It cost me $750 to get the gasket replaced on my front manifold at the local GM dealer.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||11-01-2000||01:36 AM||||Good lord!  For $750 you could have bought an entire engine!  The front manifold is a pain to change, but it really isn't all that difficult (just time consuming).  For those of you living in rusty areas you really do need to soak the bolts with WD-40 first.  I have never had to do this myself, but I have seen rusty motors before and snapping off a few bolts isn't any fun.<P>I would guesstimate 3-4 hours.....you need to factor in getting everything out of the way (AC compressor, etc.) plus reinstalling everything too....a good shop may do it faster, but will still charge you.<P>BTW....use the gaskets from a '93-'95 Camaro/Firebird 3.4 V-6.  They look different, but they work the same and are MUCH less than the Fiero ones.  I paid $6 for a set of Fel-Pro Camaro gaskets.....the Fiero versions are $23!||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||11-01-2000||03:26 AM||||it usually takes us about an hour to change the front manifold and about an hour to change the rear (but, remember, we are a shop - it's easier when the car is up on a lift!)-- everyone here is right - WD-40 or Liquid Wrench works great as does a torch for those stubborn bolts.<P>mrfiero is right about the gaskets (and the price of a new engine) too and we use Fel-Pro. <P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
